":"kaikki:38e9454b5b9fc94a98","definition":"An animal belonging to either the class Reptilia or the class Amphibia.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["herptile","herp"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"dated","register":"dated","wordFamily":["eureptile","nonreptile","reptilase","reptiledom","reptilehood","reptilekind","reptilelike","reptilic","reptiliferous","reptiliform","reptilism","reptilivorous"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reptile#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2931642ee6ba5000ac","definition":"An ectothermic, scaly animal, whether sauropsid or synapsid, of the clade Amniota.","example":"Prior to the 1990s, the non-mammalian synapsids were considered true reptiles.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["creeper","reptile"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"dated, proscribed","register":"dated, proscribed","wordFamily":["eureptile","nonreptile","reptilase","reptiledom","reptilehood","reptilekind","reptilelike","reptilic","reptiliferous","reptiliform","reptilism","reptilivorous"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reptile#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ea00a1dd3c93db2be2","definition":"An abject, grovelling, loathsome or repulsive person.","example":"This work may, indeed, be considered as a great creation of our own; and for a little reptile of a critic to presume to find fault with any of its parts, without knowing the manner in which the whole is connected, and before he comes to the final catastrophe, is a most presumptuous absurdity.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["creeper","reptile"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"dated, figuratively","register":"dated, figuratively","wordFamily":["eureptile","nonreptile","reptilase","reptiledom","reptilehood","reptilekind","reptilelike","reptilic","reptiliferous","rep